  "text": "{\n\"care_cues\": [\n  {\n    \"cue\": \"Going around the wall instead of crossing it\",\n    \"evidence\": \"In each transfer the gripper travels north to the top edge and crosses the wall line only north of the wall upper end: cup about 11-15 s, block about 40-45 s, marker about 69-73 s. It never crosses the gray vertical line in its middle section.\",\n    \"object\": \"gripper\",\n    \"t_end\": 73.0,\n    \"t_start\": 11.0\n  },\n  {\n    \"cue\": \"Sustained contact before moving an object\",\n    \"evidence\": \"The gripper stays overlapped/at the object for several seconds before the object changes position: cup about 1-10 s, blue block about 33-39 s, marker about 61-68 s. This suggests the object is secured before transport, although the reason cannot be determined.\",\n    \"object\": \"gripper\",\n    \"t_end\": 68.0,\n    \"t_start\": 1.0\n  },\n  {\n    \"cue\": \"Small, incremental movements during final placement\",\n    \"evidence\": \"Once over the tray, the gripper moves in small frame-to-frame steps for several seconds before the object appears separate: cup 17-24 s, block 46-53 s, marker 74-80 s. This is consistent with careful placement.\",\n    \"object\": \"gripper\",\n    \"t_end\": 80.0,\n    \"t_start\": 17.0\n  },\n  {\n    \"cue\": \"No visible tipping of the cup from the overhead view\",\n    \"evidence\": \"The cup square outline stays oriented the same way while it is carried and after placement, but the overhead view does not show tilt directly.\",\n    \"object\": \"cup\",\n    \"t_end\": 25.0,\n    \"t_start\": 11.0\n  }\n],\n\"events\": [\n  {\n    \"evidence\": \"At 0 s the black gripper is just north of the cup; by 1 s it is alongside/overlapping the cup. From 1-10 s the two remain together at the lower-left position. Between 10-11 s they have moved together to the upper-left.\",\n    \"object\": \"cup\",\n    \"t_end\": 10.0,\n    \"t_start\": 0.0,\n    \"type\": \"grasp\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"evidence\": \"Co-transport is first clear at 11 s in the upper-left, continues east along the top around 12-15 s, then south toward the tray at 16 s. The cup remains associated with the gripper over the tray during 17-23 s.\",\n    \"object\": \"cup\",\n    \"t_end\": 23.0,\n    \"t_start\": 11.0,\n    \"type\": \"carry\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"evidence\": \"At 24 s the yellow/white cup outline is visible separately inside the left side of the tray, and by 25 s the gripper has moved north away from the tray while the cup stays in place.\",\n    \"object\": \"cup\",\n    \"t_end\": 25.0,\n    \"t_start\": 23.0,\n    \"type\": \"release\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"evidence\": \"The gripper approaches the stationary blue block around 29-33 s. At 33 s the blue square is at the gripper edge and only a blue sliver remains visible during 34-39 s while the gripper stays in the same area.\",\n    \"object\": \"block\",\n    \"t_end\": 39.0,\n    \"t_start\": 29.0,\n    \"type\": \"grasp\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"evidence\": \"Between 39-40 s the gripper/block have moved north together. They move east along the top at 41-44 s, then south toward the tray at 45 s. The gripper remains over the tray with the blue sliver still associated during 46-52 s.\",\n    \"object\": \"block\",\n    \"t_end\": 52.0,\n    \"t_start\": 40.0,\n    \"type\": \"carry\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"evidence\": \"At 53 s the blue block is visible separately inside the tray, immediately to the right of the cup. By 54-55 s the gripper is moving away north of the tray and the block remains in the tray.\",\n    \"object\": \"block\",\n    \"t_end\": 55.0,\n    \"t_start\": 52.0,\n    \"type\": \"release\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"evidence\": \"The gripper moves south toward the red marker around 58-60 s. At 60 s it contacts the marker north end. From 61-68 s the gripper stays in place and the red marker becomes mostly hidden, with only a small red tip visible at the gripper lower edge.\",\n    \"object\": \"marker\",\n    \"t_end\": 68.0,\n    \"t_start\": 58.0,\n    \"type\": \"grasp\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"evidence\": \"The gripper/marker move north at 69-70 s, east along the top at 71-72 s, and south toward the tray at 73 s. From 74-79 s the red marker protrudes from the gripper over the right side of the tray while the gripper makes small movements.\",\n    \"object\": \"marker\",\n    \"t_end\": 79.0,\n    \"t_start\": 69.0,\n    \"type\": \"carry\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"evidence\": \"At 80 s the red marker is visible separately inside the tray to the right of the blue block and the gripper is east of the tray. By 81-82 s the gripper is farther northeast and the marker remains in the tray.\",\n    \"object\": \"marker\",\n    \"t_end\": 82.0,\n    \"t_start\": 79.0,\n    \"type\": \"release\"\n  }\n],\n\"objects\": [\n  {\n    \"description\": \"Large black vertical rectangle that moves around the tabletop and overlaps/carries the smaller objects\",\n    \"kind\": \"gripper\",\n    \"reason\": \"It is the moving agent that picks up and places the other objects\",\n    \"relevant\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"description\": \"Small square object with a white/gray rim and yellow interior, starting at lower-left; ends inside the left side of the tray\",\n    \"kind\": \"cup\",\n    \"reason\": \"It is one of the objects packed into the destination tray\",\n    \"relevant\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"description\": \"Small solid blue square, starting left of center; ends inside the tray between the cup and marker\",\n    \"kind\": \"block\",\n    \"reason\": \"It is one of the objects packed into the destination tray\",\n    \"relevant\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"description\": \"Small red elongated oval/capsule, starting upper-left of center; ends inside the right side of the tray lying diagonally\",\n    \"kind\": \"marker\",\n    \"reason\": \"It is one of the objects packed into the destination tray\",\n    \"relevant\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"description\": \"Large gray rectangular container at the upper-right, stationary throughout\",\n    \"kind\": \"tray\",\n    \"reason\": \"It is the destination into which the cup, block, and marker are placed\",\n    \"relevant\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"description\": \"Long thin gray vertical strip near the center, running from the bottom edge upward but stopping short of the top edge, leaving a gap at the north end\",\n    \"kind\": \"wall\",\n    \"reason\": \"It separates the starting side from the tray side and the gripper route goes around its upper end\",\n    \"relevant\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"description\": \"Beige rectangular tabletop surface visible under all objects, stationary background\",\n    \"kind\": \"other\",\n    \"reason\": \"It supports the objects but is not itself moved or packed\",\n    \"relevant\": false\n  }\n],\n\"summary\": \"The gripper moves three left-side objects one at a time into the gray tray on the right: first the yellow-white cup, then the blue block, then the red marker. Each transfer uses a northward route around the upper end of the central gray wall, followed by several seconds of small placement movements over the tray. By 80-82 s all three objects rest inside the tray and the gripper has moved away.\",\n\"uncertainties\": [\n  {\n    \"about\": \"Exact grasp and release instants\",\n    \"question\": \"When exactly does each grasp or release occur within the frame intervals, since frames are 1 s apart and the gripper occludes the objects?\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"about\": \"Reason for the long stationary contact phases\",\n    \"question\": \"Does the gripper remain at the cup for 1-10 s, block for 33-39 s, and marker for 61-68 s because of grip closing, alignment, waiting, or another requirement?\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"about\": \"Height, tilt, and force\",\n    \"question\": \"From the overhead frames, gripper height, object tilt/levelness, contact force, and whether the cup contents are kept level cannot be determined.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"about\": \"Reason for the northern route\",\n    \"question\": \"The route consistently goes around the top end of the wall, but the video does not settle whether this is required by the wall height, gripper limits, or a chosen path.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"about\": \"Marker orientation in 3D\",\n    \"question\": \"The top-down red oval does not settle whether the marker is standing, lying, or reoriented during carrying; it is seen diagonally in the tray at the end.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"about\": \"Possible incidental contact with the marker\",\n    \"question\": \"The red marker appears at slightly different positions around 11-12 s and 40-41 s while the gripper passes north, but the frames do not settle whether it was nudged or only occluded/redrawn.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"about\": \"Cup contents\",\n    \"question\": \"The yellow area is visible inside the cup rim, but whether it is the cup interior color or contents, and whether any contents must stay level, cannot be told from the frames.\"\n  }\n]\n}",
